  "broader": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/ins/6205",
  "definition": "Prohibited Policy Provisions",
  "effectiveDate": "2021-11-24",
  "historyNote": "#13297, eff 11-24-21",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Ins 6205.06",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins6200.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ins 6205.06 Prohibited Policy Provisions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 6205.06 Prohibited Policy Provisions.\n\n(a) Disability income benefits shall not require the loss to commence less than 30 days after the date of accident nor shall any policy that the insurer cancels or refuses to renew require that it be in force at the time the disability commences, if the accident occurred while the coverage was in force.\n\n(b) Policies providing disability income protection shall not in any way condition benefit payments for total disability on “continuous confinement within doors” or language of similar import.\n\n(c) No policy of health and accident insurance shall contain a provision that the disability period shall be considered to commence with the date on which written notice is actually received by the company.\n\n(d) Disability income benefits shall not be reduced because of an increase in benefits paid under the Social Security Act as prohibited under RSA 415:6, I(13) and RSA 415:18, I(o).\n\nSource. #13297, eff 11-24-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins6200.html"
